    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-027-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-027 — logarithmic spiral claim validation (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 77.6/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 adds synthetic k recovery sweep (max error <0.05), shuffle ablation, scipy KS on residuals, and exports mixed/supported verdict on Nautilus (log pearson r≈0.96). Conus remains mixed. Overall 77.6/100 (faithfulness 75.4, reproducibility 82.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit f1d96f32; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.x, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.x, Pillow 12.x. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 68, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_027_the_logarithmic_spiral_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-027_the-logarithmic-spiral.py at f1d96f32, image/png, 573601 B, 1540×1400 px, artifact_sha256 0a56caf122a1996d91e150e8411136dc8295a8903a0296287706e92784e44872 (sha256 0a56caf122a1996d91e150e8411136dc8295a8903a0296287706e92784e44872), spec_fingerprint 2a5f73fc968e53e30990a81294c167772f366249834cc189f759b23138dd37b2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2a5f73fc968e53e30990a81294c167772f366249834cc189f759b23138dd37b2; artifact_sha256: 0a56caf122a1996d91e150e8411136dc8295a8903a0296287706e92784e44872; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-027/nautilus_pompilius_specimen.jpg=ca3ae0f147e7cdf9..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-027/t1917_027_the_logarithmic_spiral_reference.json=ee8f5ec994ed23ec...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-027-the-logarithmic-spiral-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) Ch. XI: gnomonic shell growth preserves form; spire centreline is an equiangular (logarithmic) spiral r ∝ exp(kθ); reconstructed_in_script: Brightness-mask CV segmentation, log vs Archimedean vs power AICc, shuffle ablation, k-sweep recovery, result.json verdict; transfer_boundary: Photographic perspective and short visible whorl arc; W estimate can exceed nautiloid literature when k is fitted on partial arc; does_not_claim: Exact Thompson 1917 figure digitisation; full Raup (W,D,T) 3D surface fit." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/composer-2.5> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Digitise Thompson 1917 Fig. 237-303 shell outlines from IA scan for direct overlay (future pass).",
            "remediation needed: Fit full Raup (W,D,T) mesh alongside 2D log-spiral centreline to address Raup (1966) qualification." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.776"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
}

